## Evidence Reporting Reminder

For mature results, publish the primary metric unchanged and use a label from
the task's `complete_stage_labels`, plus `metrics.scored_complete=true` or an
equivalent task-approved authority marker. Despite the compatibility name, the
list may contain an explicitly authorized reduced mode. Preserve its actual
stage and copy ratio facts when the task contract uses them. For modes the task
marks non-mature, use task-candidate or diagnostic metadata instead of
presenting them as confirmed evidence.
For ordinary task-authorized, protocol-passed, non-suspect results, preserve the
evaluator's shared `performance` source label and every configured Pareto-axis
metric. Praxist chooses confirmed and lower-admission incubator targets
independently; do not have the Peer relabel the same result based on a guessed
final target. Explicit incubator sources remain valid only when the task
evaluator contract intentionally emits them with `incubator_axis` and
`incubator_candidate_reason`.
Also include expected versus completed protocol budget and a
`protocol_integrity_passed` signal when the evaluator exposes it. If actual work
drifts from the user-approved protocol, do not mark it as clean mature evidence.
If the task's ranking policy uses variance, confidence/lower-bound robustness,
risk, regret, or Pareto dominance, publish those robust metric fields alongside
the raw primary metric.
Set `extra.is_negative=true` and `extra.evidence_valence="negative"` for
failed, dominated, constraint-violating, non-generalizing, falsifying,
ablation-null, or protocol-invalid results. Include a compact
`extra.failure_mode` and any affected `extra.disconfirming_claim_ids` so later
PI synthesis can retrieve the negative evidence instead of repeating it.
Use the task's stage labels and protocol-intent permissions. The template
default treats preliminary evidence as immature and lets an aligned protocol
prioritize follow-up when it shares complete-protocol metric semantics and
near-complete coverage. An explicitly different user-owned protocol takes
precedence, while actual stage and effort/coverage remain visible. Lanes marked
`parent_eligible: false` never supply durable parents.
